#import "../design.typ": *

#appendix(letter: "B", title: "Glossary")

The vocabulary of knowing your book, gathered in one place.

#term("Advisory")[
  The governing principle: every intelligence observes and reports, and never edits
  your prose on its own. A change is always a diff you confirm, with your old words a
  keystroke back.
]

#term("Fact")[
  A specific, checkable claim your book rests on — a date, a name, a distance — kept in
  the Facts system book, apart from your prose, so the tool can hold it steady.
]

#term("Knowledge graph")[
  A layer of typed connections over your book — mentions, event participants,
  contradictions, citations — derived from what you wrote, walkable, and answerable with
  `graph ask`.
]

#term("Continuity (SENTINEL)")[
  The book watching *where* and *when*: co-location, timeline, numeric, character-fact
  drift, and referenced-before-introduced, in one ranked ledger.
]

#term("Grant")[
  In KEN, the earliest moment a character could know a topic — derived from timeline
  presence (they were there) or a `know:` / `reveals:` tag you place.
]

#term("Epistemic break")[
  A character using knowledge before they have it: *premature_knowledge*, a
  *leaked_secret*, or a *dropped_reveal* (knowledge set up and never spent). The axis
  KEN watches that continuity cannot.
]

#term("Read-through (LECTOR)")[
  The book read forward, once, whole, as a first reader — its *shape* (measured
  intensity vs. the framework's curve) and its *audience* experience (confusion,
  info-dump, attention-dip, put-down risk, unpaid setup).
]

#term("Distinctiveness matrix")[
  CHORUS's z-scored comparison of the whole cast's voice fingerprints — the thing that
  flags two characters who read alike.
]

#term("Milestone")[
  A snapshot of every reader's verdict at one moment (`chronicle mark`), so a later
  draft can be trended against it — cleared vs. introduced.
]

#term("Deterministic / cost-capped")[
  *Deterministic* means the tool reads your manuscript and its structure with no model,
  at no cost. Where a language model genuinely helps, it is *cost-capped* and opt-in —
  you ask, you see the estimate, the default is off.
]

#term("The worklist")[
  The Editorial Pass (`Ctrl+V Shift+R`): every reader's findings unified into one ranked
  list, each acted on with the right kind of help — a reviewed rewrite, a decision you
  make, or a brief where the structure is yours to move.
]
